---
/**
 * The ONE place the docs site says what a shared link should show
 * (roadmap 249.17, split out of 249.15).
 *
 * Before this, the built site carried ZERO `og:` and ZERO `twitter:` tags.
 * Measured on the BUILT artifact, not inferred from source: a full
 * `npm run docs:build` was run at `3e1dac1` with these files stashed, and
 * `grep -rl 'property="og:' apps/docs/dist --include='*.html'` returned **0**
 * of **138** built `index.html` files (`name="twitter:` likewise 0). The
 * source-only reading agreed and is the weaker of the two — `astro build` is
 * what turns a prop into a tag, which is the same reason this gate exists at
 * all. (A first pass grepped the looser `og:` over source and read 4 hits;
 * every one was the substring inside `dialog:` in prose. Plain fixed string
 * first, per CLAUDE.md.) So a link to any docs page pasted into a chat
 * rendered as a bare URL with whatever text the platform guessed.
 *
 * WHY A COMPONENT AND NOT TWELVE COPIES. Twelve source files own a `<head>`
 * here — `Gallery.astro` plus eleven pages that deliberately do not use it
 * (the RF profile documents, the isolated component demos, the full-screen
 * schedule, the landing page). `PrefBootstrap.astro`'s header records what
 * happens when head logic is copied instead: its two copies disagreed on the
 * default density, and a first-time visitor measurably got a different
 * density on the landing page than on every docs page. Same head, same
 * hazard, same answer.
 *
 * NO `og:image` YET, deliberately. The card image is the half of 249.15 that
 * stays open: its evidence is a rendered image a human compares, which
 * `.roundtable/ENVIRONMENT.md`'s first list says a cloud wake cannot take.
 * `twitter:card` is therefore `summary` — the small-card form that needs no
 * image — rather than the `summary_large_image` the image half will switch it
 * to. Claiming the large card while shipping no image is a claim the artifact
 * does not support.
 *
 * `title` is the FULL document title, passed rather than re-derived, because
 * the twelve heads do not spell it the same way: `Gallery.astro` renders
 * `{title} · busy-office-ui` while every self-head page writes its own
 * complete string. The gate asserts `og:title` equals what the built page's
 * `<title>` actually says, so a caller that passes something else fails
 * rather than drifting quietly.
 *
 * `canonical` is derived here from Astro's route and asserted in
 * `check-metadata.mjs` against the url `dist-pages.mjs` produces by WALKING
 * `dist/`. Two independent derivations, neither able to see the other — the
 * same reconciliation shape arm 3 (sitemap vs. dist walk) already uses, and
 * for the same reason: a canonical URL generated from the dist walk and then
 * checked against the dist walk would be green no matter what broke.
 */
const { title, description } = Astro.props;

if (typeof title !== 'string' || title.trim().length === 0) {
  throw new Error(
    `SocialMeta on ${Astro.url.pathname}: needs the page's full document title, ` +
      'the same string its <title> renders — check-metadata.mjs asserts the two agree.',
  );
}
/* Gallery.astro already throws below 40 characters and check-metadata.mjs
   asserts it on the built page; this is not a third opinion on the floor, only
   a refusal to emit an og:description that is absent or empty. */
if (typeof description !== 'string' || description.trim().length === 0) {
  throw new Error(`SocialMeta on ${Astro.url.pathname}: needs the page's meta description.`);
}

/* dist-pages.mjs yields every url with a trailing slash, and that is the form
   the sitemap and check-metadata.mjs compare against. Normalise here rather
   than in the gate: a gate that trims both sides before comparing cannot see a
   real mismatch. */
const pathname = Astro.url.pathname.endsWith('/') ? Astro.url.pathname : `${Astro.url.pathname}/`;
const canonical = new URL(pathname, Astro.site).href;
---
<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
<meta property="og:site_name" content="busy-office-ui" />
<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
<meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
